VIUA-LD(1) "Viua VM PUT_VIUAVM_VERSION_HERE" "Viua VM Manual"

# NAME

viua-ld - the Viua VM linker

# SYNOPSIS

*viua ld* [*--out* _output_] [*--type* _type_] _baseobj_ [_objfile_...]

# DESCRIPTION

Link ELF files containing Viua bytecode.

# OPTIONS

include(common/tool-options.scdoc)

*-o*, *--out*=_output_
	Write produced file into _output_ file instead of the default output path.
	The default output path depends on the type of the produced ELF:
	- *a.out* for executable files
	- _baseobj_.so for shared libraries
	- _baseobj_.a for static libraries
	- _baseobj_.o for object files

*--type*=_type_
	Produce an ELF of the requested type. The _type_ may be one of:
	- *exec* (the default) to produce an executable file
	- *shared* to produce a shared library
	- *static* to produce a static library
	- *object* to produce an object file

*-c*, *--object*
	A shortcut for *--type object*.

*--dump*=_what_
	Dump results of the intermediate stages of the linking process. The _what_
	argument may be:
	- *strtab* to dump the string table

*--comment*=_value_
	Set contents of the *.comment* section to _value_.

*-i*, *--interpreter*=_interpreter_
	Set _interpreter_ as the requested program interpreter in the *.interp*
	section.

*--build-id*=_style_
	Create a ".note.gnu.build-id" ELF note section, uniquely identifying a
	linked file. _style_ can be either of:

[[ _style_
:[ bits
:< comment
|  *sha1*
:  160
:  SHA1
|  *sha256*
:  256
:  SHA2
|  *sha384*
:  384
:  SHA2
|  *sha512*
:  512
:  SHA2
|  *blake2b*
:  32-512
:  BLAKE2B, by default 512 bits (see *--build-id-size*)
|  *blake3*
:  32-unlimited
:  BLAKE3, by default 256 bits (see *--build-id-size*)
|  *none*
:  -
:  explicitly disables .note.gnu.build-id

	For hash-based build IDs, the whole file contents are hashed, with the space
	reserved for the digest zeroed out.

*--build-id-size*=_size_
	Set the size of the digest for *blake2b* or *blake3* build IDs. The size
	must be divisible by 8.

; - *sha1*
; - *sha256*
; - *sha384*
; - *sha512*
; - *uuid*
; - *none*

# EXIT STATUS

|[ 0
:< Successful program execution
|  1
:  Invalid input

# FILES

|[ _baseobj_
:< The main object file to use. Default name of the output depends on it.
|  _objfiles_
:  The object files to link with the main file.
|  _output_
:  The produced ELF file.

The linker opens its input files read-only.

# SEE ALSO

*viua-asm*(1),
*viua-dis*(1),
*viua-readelf*(1).

*readelf*(1),
*elf*(5).

